  "body": "## Summary\n\nFinish the skill correction left open by PR #3031 and the issue comment from 2026-11-20T16:38:40Z.\n\n- Remove face alignment and program metadata from the remaining gaps.\n- Keep the existing units and face-lay rows. Add the shipped `set_program` status.\n- Link `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md`. Document `camcraft-cli mcp reference` and `camcraft-cli mcp prompt`.\n- Add two drift pins and a scanner control to the existing `mcp_doc_drift` binary. Keep its six existing tests.\n- Record the bounded decision in `docs/decisions/1947-mcp-gap-drift.md`.\n\nThe scanner compares identifiers with the live tool catalog. It handles snake_case, CamelCase and single-word tools in code spans. Ordinary prose such as \"post\" or \"undo\" does not become a tool name. The scanner stops at the next section or separator.\n\n## Readings\n\nBase: `8a605c4fc00a0c8835e32775aa9db70facb4e45f` from upstream `main`.\n\nThe current tool table includes `set_units`, `set_program` and `lay_part_on_face`. Their handlers use the corresponding undoable commands. The existing catalog and local prompt already derive from that table. No catalog regeneration or runtime change is needed.\n\nPRs #4066, #4040, #4022 and #3617 change other skill rows. They do not change these status, reference or gap sections, or this drift binary.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Red: `cargo test -j 3 -p camcraft-app --test mcp_doc_drift` against the unchanged skill: seven passed, two failed.\n  - `the_known_gaps_name_no_shipped_tool` found `post`, `set_part_axes`, `lay_part_on_points`, `lay_part_on_face` and `set_wcs_from_features`.\n  - `the_skill_links_the_generated_reference_and_local_prompt` found the missing reference link.\n- Green: the same binary passes all nine tests after the correction. None is ignored.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base 8a605c4fc00a0c8835e32775aa9db70facb4e45f`: PASS. One actual step runs all nine drift tests.\n- `python3 -B -m unittest discover -s .claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/tests -v`: PASS, 14 tests.\n- `python3 -B -m unittest discover -s site/tests -p test_ai_guide.py -v`: PASS, four tests.\n- Focused link, current CLI dispatch, unique status-row and baseline-format checks: PASS, four checks.\n- `git diff --check`: PASS.\n- Default `rustfmt --check` reports the same formatting differences on the base file. The added code introduces no further differences. No unrelated formatting changed.\n\n## Limits\n\nNo production source, tool schema, tool handler, output, geometry, safety check or golden changes.\n\nThe universal light-lane rule was not exercised. This bounded documentation/test correction does not change code covered by that release-mode lane. No light, heavy, batch, release, GUI, catalog, importer or fixture build ran. Only the affected test target and the gate driver compiled. No physical machine or live agent client was exercised. Graphify is not on PATH; no graph update ran.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: medium\nProcess change: yes\n\nFixes #1947\n",
